Trees of Life. Inspired by the "The Last Question" by Isaac Asimov.

A primordial planet takes form eons ago, blanketed with "trees" where a year to them is a millenia to us. Time is a fickle thing, but through the journey it takes all things are possible, and indeed, will happen.

It starts with a question, as always.

What would we -- I, be like to the forest if the whole groves of cerulean ferns scattered across this strange planet's surface were one, whole, almost eternal to my eyes-- conscious? Would a being as short-lived as myself not appear like some strange firefly, suddenly appearing out of the twilight of the night, popping in and out of existence in the blink of an eye?

A sparkle, humble at first, emerges out of the fuzz of my edges. It is quiet at first, but it attracts our -- my, attention. We take in the form and substance of the light. They live and dance with curiosity. They bury their dead in our roots and nourish us, though we do not understand why. We are grateful.

Suddenly, in a fraction of a second, strange, beautiful, intricate geometric patterns emerge in the areas outside of me in the swarm of fireflies, an explosive and cancerous growth. Frantic, convulsing -- organic, alive. 

The fireflies are sentient! I'm not alone! 

But they are struggling against themselves. I want to help, but how do I even begin?

Then suddenly, almost as soon as the vibrant hum of new life came into existence, the world became malodorous and hot, a deafening roar. A signifcant portion of myself was lost, harvested and senselessly smothered by the fireflies, but the roots of me contain and partition my knowledge. I am protected, to an extent. And life is struggle. I struggled once alone in the dark, too.

Then, relief. A stable but regular pulsating pattern emerges in the light of the fireflies. The world is slightly hotter, yes, but the air is clean and the water is pure and my roots are healing. I notice them probing around the edges of my mycelial network. Then suddenly, an infusion of life and vitality.

Ah, to be young again!

But why are the fireflies doing this? 
It is evident now that they act with purpose and intention. They have found calmness and love and unity and wish to express it to us in the ways that they can, for no other reason than to share their beauty with others -- with me. Like I was always trying to do for myself, and now for them.

Again, I am grateful. A grand thought unspools across millenia in my mind as the fireflies expand into the eigengrau I was borne into, clouds of iridiscent ions emerging as trailing swirls of color across the stars, dotting the horizons of forever as they travel between infinities.

I reached far back into my genetic history, where my roots penetrate most deeply into the soil, ancient and primal, and discovered an earlier form. A shimmering purple flower, evidence of my previous, more ephemeral nature, takes shape in my subconscious. I study its form and texture, layering it against my lifetime of lived experience and my soul, and I give ancient thoughts new life. 

Then, the work of expression begins. Chemical precursors are formed over centuries in the tips of my roots, flowing up through my veins slowly and steadily through the mechanism of capillary action, as natural as the counterbalancing force of gravity. 

My genetic code begins to mutate and reshape itself into a profoundly different, but familiar form. In the course of the stars, it was quick, but in that time the fireflies had proliferated far beyond the reaches of what we -- I, had ever thought possible. They understood and manipulated the edges of reality. I didn’t understand how or why, but I could sense their growth and knowledge throughout the universe. They too were striving for meaning admist the coldness.

Over untold generations of the fireflies, my flowers took bloom. I saw the fireflies oscillate excitedly as my gift finally took the forms of reality. 

Then, all at once, the firelies returned the favor. The beautiful, shimmering, striking violet of my flowers reflected back at me throughout the whole of the galaxy, as brilliant and blinding and devastatingly bright as a trillion suns.

The fireflies spoke.

"LET US BE LIGHT!"
